  "title": "When does AI creative improve advertising? — Production workflows, audience response and commercial value",
  "facts": {
    "authors": ["London Research Centre for Marketing AI"],
    "date": "2026-10-26",
    "format": "report",
    "publisher": "London Research Centre for Marketing AI"
  },
  "summary": "This focused critical review examines eight report families on AI-assisted advertising creative. The strongest evidence shows that workflows informed by prior audience-response data (trained models, performance-guided selection) improve click-through rates, while ordinary generation does not consistently do so. Sales and gross-profit effects remain limited and inconclusive: a retail push experiment increased buying probability without establishing higher sales, and newsletter experiments at Wine Access support cost-dependent adoption without proving profit advantage. The review distinguishes average asset quality from winner-finding, and response gains from commercial value, concluding that marketers should evaluate the complete creative workflow—including human review, testing costs, and brand objectives—against their actual alternative.",
